The original GNU Go regression tools.

These scripts come from the autotools era of GNU Go. They still work
but are no longer needed for normal testing: tests/run_tests.py and
ctest do the same with Python only (see tests/README).

Run them from the tests/ directory. They use the engine named by the
GNUGO environment variable, by default ../build/src/interface/gnugo:

  cd tests
  GNUGO=../build/src/interface/gnugo sh ../contrib/regress/eval.sh blunder.tst
  sh ../contrib/regress/regress.sh . blunder.tst
  pike ../contrib/regress/regress.pike --engine ../build/src/interface/gnugo owl
  pike ../contrib/regress/view.pike strategy:40

  regress.sh, eval.sh,   run one suite and report its results (awk)
  test.sh, regress.awk
  eval3.sh, regress.pl,  HTML views of the regression results (Perl, CGI)
  regress.plx
  regress.pike           run suites in parallel with timing statistics (Pike)
  view.pike              inspect a test case on a graphical board (Pike, GTK)
  regress.cmd            Windows version of regress.sh (needs awk)
  BREAKAGE               log of test results that changed between versions
  breakage2tst.py        update .tst files from BREAKAGE (Python 2)

The Texinfo manual, chapter "Regression", describes them in detail.
